WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.652
Welcome to the government modules tour.

2
00:00:02.652 --> 00:00:13.802
SaloneHCM's Gov tier adds the controls public payroll demands: a civil service salary structure, establishment discipline, budget checks before money moves, and public transparency.

3
00:00:13.802 --> 00:00:15.034
Let's tour each one.

4
00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:22.414
The civil service module holds your grade and step salary matrix, allowance rules, and budget codes.

5
00:00:22.414 --> 00:00:32.399
Salaries flow from the structure — not from ad-hoc numbers — so a grade seven step three officer in Bo earns exactly what the structure says, same as in Freetown.

6
00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:35.666
Retro-pay and ghost-worker audit tools live here too.

7
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:41.877
Establishment control compares approved posts against filled posts, ministry by ministry.

8
00:00:41.877 --> 00:00:49.906
Over-establishment hiring gets flagged before it becomes a payroll liability, and vacancies are visible for workforce planning.

9
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:20.949
Before any payroll run commits, the budget check verifies there's allocation left on every budget code the run will consume.

10
00:01:20.949 --> 00:01:26.971
If a code is over, the run is blocked — and only a documented override with a reason can proceed.

11
00:01:26.971 --> 00:01:32.186
On the payroll page, the budget balances panel shows exactly where each code stands.

12
00:01:53.250 --> 00:02:04.980
Finally, the open-gov transparency portal — a public page, no login required — publishing aggregate payroll statistics for your ministry: headcount, wage bill trends, and grade distributions.

13
00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.402
Citizens and journalists see the numbers; personal data stays protected.

14
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:16.786
Structure, establishment, budget discipline, and daylight — the four pillars of clean government payroll.

15
00:02:16.786 --> 00:02:22.202
Take the government modules quiz in the Training Center to complete your certification.
